From e89e00ee14b34e18b3d3f488314c8b5de2a2472b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francois Massot-Pellet <francois.massot-pellet@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:05:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Rename the rfnm transport to shiva; support the NXP
 la93xx_freertos HIF

The transport is not RFNM specific: it works on any host with the NXP
la9310shiva driver, including the LimeSDR-Micro on an i.MX95 with the
NXP BSP.

- rfnm_port.py -> shiva_port.py, RfnmPort -> ShivaPort; rfnm_port.py
  stays as a compatibility alias and --transport rfnm still works.
- Pick the sw_cmd_desc location from DCFG SCRATCHRW[3] (HIF offset
  published by the NXP firmware): NXP tree HIF at TCML+0x1B000 with
  sw_cmd_desc at +0x240, RFNM tree TCML+0x1C000 / +0x218 (default).
  SHIVA_HIF_OFFSET / SHIVA_SW_CMD_OFFSET override.
- Map CCSR/TCML/TCMU through /dev/shiva0 when the driver accepts it
  (la93xx_host_sw modinfo mmap patch), fall back to /dev/mem.
- SHIVA_DEVICE env (RFNM_SHIVA_DEVICE still accepted).
- docs/rfnm.md -> docs/shiva.md, README tables, tests renamed plus HIF
  layout tests.
