new file mode 100644
index 0000000..268932c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/shiva.md
@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@
+# la9310shiva hosts (`shiva` transport): RFNM and LimeSDR-Micro on the NXP BSP
+
+The debugger runs on any host that drives the LA9310 with the NXP
+`la9310shiva` kernel driver, using the `shiva` transport:
+
+- RFNM board (i.MX8M Plus host, RFNM la93xx_freertos);
+- LimeSDR-Micro on an i.MX95 FRDM with the NXP BSP (NXP la93xx_freertos).
+
+Every self-hosted feature works: attach, memory reads while streaming,
+breakpoints, watchpoints that name the writer, profiling, and `load`.
+
+`--transport rfnm` and `rfnm_port.py` are kept as aliases of
+`--transport shiva` and `shiva_port.py`.
+
+## How it connects
+
+| | LimeSDR-Micro, LimeSuiteNG (`selfhosted`) | la9310shiva hosts (`shiva`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Kernel driver | `la9310_limesdr` | `la9310shiva` (`/dev/shiva0`) |
+| Finding the windows | fixed mmap window ids on the driver node | `IOCTL_LA93XX_MODINFO_GET` returns the host physical addresses of CCSR, TCML and TCMU |
+| Mapping | mmap of the driver node | mmap of `/dev/shiva0` when the driver accepts the PCIe BARs (la93xx_host_sw modinfo mmap patch), else `/dev/mem` (`O_SYNC`) |
+| M4 request block | `struct vspa_dbg_proxy`, address published in DCFG SCRATCHRW32 | `sw_cmd_desc` in the HIF, command `LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG` |
+| Doorbell | MSG unit MSIIR3 | MSG unit 2 MSIIR (CCSR + 0x1FC0008) |
+| Words per request | up to 256 | up to 28 (sw_cmd data area: 32 words) |
+
+Where `sw_cmd_desc` is depends on the firmware tree:
+
+| Firmware | HIF | `sw_cmd_desc` |
+|---|---|---|
+| RFNM la93xx_freertos | TCML + 0x1C000 | TCML + 0x1C218 |
+| NXP la93xx_freertos | TCML + 0x1B000 | TCML + 0x1B240 |
+
+The NXP firmware publishes the HIF offset in DCFG SCRATCHRW[3];
+`ShivaPort` reads it and picks the layout, and falls back to the RFNM
+layout otherwise. Override with `SHIVA_HIF_OFFSET` and
+`SHIVA_SW_CMD_OFFSET` (offset of `sw_cmd_desc` inside the HIF).
+
+Request layout in `sw_cmd_desc.data[]`, written before the status is set
+to POSTED and the doorbell rung:
+
+| word | host writes | M4 writes back |
+|---|---|---|
+| `data[0]` | op word: bits 7-0 op (1 read, 2 write), bit 8 fixed address, bits 23-16 count | error code (0 = ok) |
+| `data[1]` | debug-block byte offset | - |
+| `data[2..]` | write values | read values |
+
+The M4 sets `status = DONE (5)` last. `shiva_port.ShivaPort` has the same
+interface as `selfhosted.M4Proxy`, so all the tools use it unchanged.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- M4 firmware with the `LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG` sw_cmd handler and the
+  sw_cmd engine started:
+  - RFNM: la9310-freertos patch 0001 from la931x_iqplayer `doc/patches`;
+  - NXP la93xx_freertos (LimeSDR-Micro): patch
+    `0004-sw_cmd_engine-LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG-proxy-for-the-V.patch`
+    from la931x_iqplayer `doc/patches/la93xx_freertos`.
+- `la9310shiva.ko` loaded; run as root. With the la93xx_host_sw modinfo
+  mmap patch `/dev/mem` is not needed (works with `CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM`).
+- Python 3 on the board. Copy this repository to the board (or its NFS
+  root); the VSPA toolchain is only needed for source lines and
+  disassembly.
+
+## Use
+
+```sh
+python3 shiva_port.py heartbeat        # M4 answers VSPA debug requests
+python3 shiva_port.py info             # VSPA state snapshot
+python3 vdbg.py --transport shiva --attach /lib/firmware/apm-iqplayer-1T1R.eld
+python3 profile.py --transport shiva <firmware.eld> --seconds 10
+python3 shiva_port.py load <firmware.eld>   # reload a hung VSPA
+```
+
+`shiva_port.py` takes the same verbs as `selfhosted.py`. Override the
+device with `SHIVA_DEVICE` (`RFNM_SHIVA_DEVICE` still accepted), and the
+request size with `VSPA_DBG_MAX_WORDS` (at most 28).
+
+## Status on hardware
+
+imx95frdm + LimeSDR-Micro, NXP BSP, NXP la93xx_freertos with
+la931x_iqplayer `doc/patches/la93xx_freertos` 0001-0005, iqplayer 1T1R:
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `shiva_port.py heartbeat` | OK |
+| `shiva_port.py info` (running core) | OK: RUNNING, `idbg_en=0`, IP regs not readable until a halt or breakpoint |
+| `vdbg.py --attach`, `dmem` while streaming | OK, words change while TX/RX stream |
+| `profile.py` idle | OK: 100% `___internal_done` (event-driven VSPA sleeps between passes) |
+| `profile.py` TX + RX streaming, 10 s | OK: 667 samples, `_PUSH_RX_DATA` 24%, `_PUSH_TX_DATA` 23%, `_meter_end` 13%, `_VSPA_PROXY_update` 9%, idle 6% |
+| `break _PUSH_RX_DATA`, `continue` | OK: stopped at `0x10B8 <_PUSH_RX_DATA> at iqmod_rx.c:353` |
+| `regs` while halted, clear + `continue`, `detach`, `load`, `--transport rfnm` | not recorded yet |
+
+The RFNM board has only the offline tests so far.
+
+## Example: halt in the RX path
+
+During streaming:
+
+```
+(vdbg) dmem <addr> 4          # live read, the core keeps running
+(vdbg) break _PUSH_RX_DATA
+(vdbg) continue
+stopped: breakpoint/comparator 0
+  0x10B8 <_PUSH_RX_DATA> at iqmod_rx.c:353
+```
+
+Get buffer addresses from the ELF (`print &input_qec_buffer`); they
+depend on the build. Words that read `DEADBEEF` were not written since
+boot (crt0 fills DMEM with that pattern). `watch <addr> w dma` halts on
+the first DMA write to a word.
+
+The watchpoint compares the address, not the value, and halting stops the
+stream; restore with `shiva_port.py load <eld>`.
+
+## Tests
+
+`tests/test_shiva_port.py` checks the request layout, the HIF layout
+selection, chunking, error and timeout handling against an in-memory
+TCML/CCSR and a simulated M4 (no board needed).
